# unlit.fmat — self-lit, as a material.
#
# This was `unlit: true` on an entity attachment, and nothing else in the engine
# could reach it: a brush face had no such field. As a material any surface can
# have it.
#
# It takes no texture of its own, so the surface keeps whatever art it names and
# simply stops being shaded. Fog still applies, and the surface goes to the
# blended pass — which is what lets a texture's own alpha fade it off at the
# edges.
kind: surface
doc: No light, no shadow — the texture's own colour. A beam, a readout, a sign.
effects:
  - effect: unlit
